1. Is the input actually controlled by an external user (e.g., network input, file content, environment variable)?
2. Does the data flow from the source to the sink without proper sanitization or validation?
3. Are there any input validation checks (length limits, character whitelists, escaping) before the command execution?
4. Could an attacker inject shell metacharacters like ; | & ` $ ( ) to execute arbitrary commands?
5. Is the command execution wrapped in any sandboxing or privilege-dropping mechanism?
